{
  "title": "68: al-Qalam القلم",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful.\nنٓ وَالْقَلَمِ وَمَا يَسْطُرُونَ (1)\nNAA WAL QALAME WA MAA YASTUROONA.\nNoon. I swear by the pen and what the angels write,\nمَآ اَنتَ بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ بِمَجْنُونٍ (2)\nMAA AANTA BE-NE’MATE RABBEKA BEMAJNOONIN.\nBy the grace of your Lord you are not mad.\nوَاِنَّ لَكَ لَاَجْرًا غَيْرَ مَمْنُونٍ (3)\nWA INNA LAKA LAAJRAN GHAYRA MAMNOONIN.\nAnd most surely you shall have a reward never to be cut off.\nوَاِنَّكَ لَعَلَىٰ خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ (4)\nWA LAA’ALAA KHULUQIN A’AZEEMIN.\nAnd most surely you conform (yourself) to sublime morality.\nفَسَتُبْصِرُ وَيُبْصِرُونَ (5)\nFASATUBSERU WAYUBSEROONA.\nSo you shall see, and they (too) shall see,\nبِاَييِّكُمُ الْمَفْتُونُ (6)\nBEAAYYYEKUMU AL-MAFTOONU.\nWhich of you is afflicted with madness.\nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَن ضَلَّ عَن سَبِيلِهِۦ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُهْتَدِينَ (7)\nINNAL RABBAKA HOWA A-A’LAMO BEMAN ZALLA A’AN SABEELEHE WA HOWA A-A’LAMO BIL-MUHTADEENA.\nSurely your Lord best knows him who errs from His way, and He best knows the followers of the right course.\nفَلَا تُطِعِ الْمُكَذِّبِينَ (8)\nFALAA LAA AL-MUKAZZEBEENA.\nSo do not yield to the rejecters.\nوَدُّوا۟ لَوْ تُدْهِنُ فَيُدْهِنُونَ (9)\nWADDOOA LAW TUDHENU FAYUDHENOONA.\nThey wish that you should be pliant so they (too) would be pliant.\nوَلَا تُطِعْ كُلَّ حَلَّافٍ مَّهِينٍ (10)\nWA LAA TO-TE’ KULLA HALLAAFIN MMAHEENIN.\nAnd yield not to any mean swearer\nهَمَّازٍ مَّشَّآءٍۭ بِنَمِيمٍ (11)\nHAMMAAZIN MMASSHAAIN BENAMEEMIN.\nDefamer, going about with slander\nمَّنَّاعٍ لِّلْخَيْرِ مُعْتَدٍ اَثِيمٍ (12)\nMMANNAAA’IN LLELKHAYRE MO’TADIN AASEEMIN.\nForbidder of good, outstepping the limits, sinful,\nعُتُلٍّۭ بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ زَنِيمٍ (13)\nU’UTULLIN BA’DA ZAALEKA ZANEEMIN.\nIgnoble, besides all that, base-born;\nاَن كَانَ ذَا مَالٍ وَبَنِينَ (14)\nAAN KAANA ZAL MAALIN WABANEENA.\nBecause he possesses wealth and sons.\nاِذَا تُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْهِ ءَايٰتُنَا قَالَ اَسٰطِيرُ الْاَوَّلِينَ (15)\nEZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHE AAYAATUNAA QAALA AASAATEERU AL-AAWLEENA.\nWhen Our communications are recited to him, he says: Stories of those of yore.\nسَنَسِمُهُۥ عَلَى الْخُرْطُومِ (16)\nSANASEMUHU A’LAL AL-KHURTOOME.\nWe will brand him on the nose.\nاِنَّا بَلَوْنٰهُمْ كَمَا بَلَوْنَآ اَصْحٰبَ الْجَنَّةِ اِذْ اَقْسَمُوا۟ لَيَصْرِمُنَّهَا مُصْبِحِينَ (17)\nINNAA BALAWNAAHUM KAMAA BALAWNAA MASALAN JANNAH IZ AAQSAMOOA LAYASREMUNNAHAA MUSBEHEENA.\nSurely We will try them as We tried the owners of the garden, when they swore that they would certainly cut off the produce in the morning,\nوَلَا يَسْتَثْنُونَ (18)\nWA LAA YASTASNOONA.\nAnd were not willing to set aside a portion (for the poor).\nفَطَافَ عَلَيْهَا طَآئِفٌ مِّن رَّبِّكَ وَهُمْ نَآئِمُونَ (19)\nFATAAFA A’LAYHAA TAAEFUN MMEN RABBEKA WA HUM NAAEMOONA.\nThen there encompassed it a visitation from your Lord while they were sleeping.\nفَاَصْبَحَتْ كَالصَّرِيمِ (20)\nFAASBAHAT KAALSSAREEME.\nSo it became as black, barren land.\nفَتَنَادَوْا۟ مُصْبِحِينَ (21)\nFATANAADAWA MUSBEHEENA.\nAnd they called out to each other in the morning,\nاَنِ اغْدُوا۟ عَلَىٰ حَرْثِكُمْ اِن كُنتُمْ صٰرِمِينَ (22)\nSAALEHAN AGHDOOA A’LAA HARSEKUM AEN KUNTUM SAAREMEENA.\nSaying: Go early to your tilth if you would cut (the produce).\nفَانطَلَقُوا۟ وَهُمْ يَتَخٰفَتُونَ (23)\nFAANTALAQOOA WA HUM YATAKHAAFATOONA.\nSo they went, while they consulted together secretly,\nاَن لَّا يَدْخُلَنَّهَا الْيَوْمَ عَلَيْكُم مِّسْكِينٌ (24)\nAAN LAA YADKHULANNAHAA YAWMA A’ALAYKUM MMESKEENUN.\nSaying: No poor man shall enter it today upon you.\nوَغَدَوْا۟ عَلَىٰ حَرْدٍ قٰدِرِينَ (25)\nWAGHADAWA A’LAA HARDIN QAADEREENA.\nAnd in the morning they went, having the power to prevent.\nفَلَمَّا رَاَوْهَا قَالُوٓا۟ اِنَّا لَضَآلُّونَ (26)\nFALAMMAA RAAWHAA QAALOOA INNAA LAZAALLOONA.\nBut when they saw it, they said: Most surely we have gone astray\nبَلْ نَحْنُ مَحْرُومُونَ (27)\nBAL NAHNO MAHROOMOONA.\nNay! we are made to suffer privation.\nقَالَ اَوْسَطُهُمْ اَلَمْ اَقُل لَّكُمْ لَوْلَا تُسَبِّحُونَ (28)\nQAALA AAWSATUHUM ALAM AQUL LAKUM LAWLAA TUSABBEHOONA.\nThe best of them said: Did I not say to you, Why do you not glorify (Allah)?\nقَالُوا۟ سُبْحٰنَ رَبِّنَآ اِنَّا كُنَّا ظٰلِمِينَ (29)\nQAALUD LAAHE RABBENAA INNAA KUNNAA ZAALEMEENA.\nThey said: Glory be to our Lord, surely we were unjust.\nفَاَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ يَتَلٰوَمُونَ (30)\nFAAQBALA KHALAA A’LAA ELAA YATALAAWAMOONA.\nThen some of them advanced against others, blaming each other.\nقَالُوا۟ يٰوَيْلَنَآ اِنَّا كُنَّا طٰغِينَ (31)\nQAALUD YAAWAYLANAA INNAA KUNNAA TAAGHEENA.\nSaid they: O woe to us! surely we were inordinate:\nعَسَىٰ رَبُّنَآ اَن يُبْدِلَنَا خَيْرًا مِّنْهَآ اِنَّآ اِلَىٰ رَبِّنَا رٰغِبُونَ (32)\nA’ASAA RABBUNAA AAN YUBDELANAA KHAYRAN MMENHAA AENNAA AELAA RABBENAA RAAGHEBOONA.\nMaybe, our Lord will give us instead one better than it; surely to our Lord do we make our humble petition.\nكَذٰلِكَ الْعَذَابُ وَلَعَذَابُ الْءَاخِرَةِ اَكْبَرُ لَوْ كَانُوا۟ يَعْلَمُونَ (33)\nKAZAALEKA A’ZAABO LA-A’ZAABUL AL-AAKHERATE AKBARO LAW KAANOOA YAA’LAMOONA.\nSuch is the chastisement, and certainly the chastisement of the hereafter is greater, did they but know!\nاِنَّ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ عِندَ رَبِّهِمْ جَنّٰتِ النَّعِيمِ (34)\nINNAL LIL-MUTTAQEENA E’ENDA RABBEHIM JANNATIN AN-NAE’EEME.\nSurely those who guard (against evil) shall have with their Lord gardens of bliss.\nاَفَنَجْعَلُ الْمُسْلِمِينَ كَالْمُجْرِمِينَ (35)\nAAFANAJA’ALU AL-MUSLEMEENA KAALMUJREMEENA.\nWhat! shall We then make (that is, treat) those who submit as the guilty?\nمَا لَكُمْ كَيْفَ تَحْكُمُونَ (36)\nMAA LAKUM KAYFA TAHKUMOONA.\nWhat has happened to you? How do you judge?\nاَمْ لَكُمْ كِتٰبٌ فِيهِ تَدْرُسُونَ (37)\nAM LAKUM KETAABUM FEEHE TADRUSOONA.\nOr have you a book wherein you read,\nاِنَّ لَكُمْ فِيهِ لَمَا تَخَيَّرُونَ (38)\nINNAL LAKUM FEEHE LAMAA TAKHAYROONA.\nThat you have surely therein what you choose?\nاَمْ لَكُمْ اَيْمٰنٌ عَلَيْنَا بٰلِغَةٌ اِلَىٰ يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ اِنَّ لَكُمْ لَمَا تَحْكُمُونَ (39)\nAM LAKUM AAYMAANUN A’LAYNAA BAALEGHATUN AELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE INNAL LAKUM LAMAA TAHKUMOONA.\nOr have you received from Us an agreement confirmed by an oath extending to the day of resurrection that you shall surely have what you demand?\nسَلْهُمْ اَيُّهُم بِذٰلِكَ زَعِيمٌ (40)\nSALHUM AAYHUM BE-ZAALEKA ZAE’EEMUN.\nAsk them which of them will vouch for that,\nاَمْ لَهُمْ شُرَكَآءُ فَلْيَاْتُوا۟ بِشُرَكَآئِهِمْ اِن كَانُوا۟ صٰدِقِينَ (41)\nAM LAHUM SHURAKAAU FALYAATOOA BE-SHORAKAAA-EHIM AEN KAANOOA SAADEQEENA.\nOr have they associates if they are truthful.\nيَوْمَ يُكْشَفُ عَن سَاقٍ وَيُدْعَوْنَ اِلَى السُّجُودِ فَلَا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ (42)\nYAWMA YUKSHAFU A’AN SAAQIN WAYUDA’AWNA ELAL AS-SUJOODE FALAA YASTATEEU’OONA.\nOn the day when there shall be a severe affliction, and they shall be called upon to make obeisance, but they shall not be able,\nخٰشِعَةً اَبْصٰرُهُمْ تَرْهَقُهُمْ ذِلَّةٌ وَقَدْ كَانُوا۟ يُدْعَوْنَ اِلَى السُّجُودِ وَهُمْ سٰلِمُونَ (43)\nKHAASHEA’ATAN AABSAARUHUM TARHAQUHUM ZELLATUN WA QAD KAANOOA YUDA’AWNA ELAL AS-SUJOODE WA HUM SAALEMOONA.\nTheir looks cast down, abasement shall overtake them; and they were called upon to make obeisance indeed while yet they were safe.\nفَذَرْنِى وَمَن يُكَذِّبُ بِهٰذَا الْحَدِيثِ سَنَسْتَدْرِجُهُم مِّنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ (44)\nFAZARNEAA WAMAN YOKAZZEBO BEHAAZAA AL-HADEESE SANASTADREJUHUM MIN HAYSO LAA YAA’LAMOONA.\nSo leave Me and him who rejects this announcement; We will overtake them by degrees, from whence they perceive not:\nوَاُمْلِى لَهُمْ اِنَّ كَيْدِى مَتِينٌ (45)\nWAAMLEAA LAHUM INNA KAYDEAA MATEENUN.\nAnd I do bear with them, surely My plan is firm.\nاَمْ تَسَْٔلُهُمْ اَجْرًا فَهُم مِّن مَّغْرَمٍ مُّثْقَلُونَ (46)\nAM TASLUHUM AJRAN FAHUM MMEN MMAGHRAMIN MMUSQALOONA.\nOr do you ask from them a reward, so that they are burdened with debt?\nاَمْ عِندَهُمُ الْغَيْبُ فَهُمْ يَكْتُبُونَ (47)\nAM E’ENDAHUMU AL-GHAYBU FAHUM YAKTUBOONA.\nOr have they (the knowledge of) the unseen, so that they write (it) down?\nفَاصْبِرْ لِحُكْمِ رَبِّكَ وَلَا تَكُن كَصَاحِبِ الْحُوتِ اِذْ نَادَىٰ وَهُوَ مَكْظُومٌ (48)\nFAS-BIR LE HUKME RABBEKA WA LAA TAKUN KASAAHEBE AL-HOOTE IZ NAADAA WA HOWA MAKZOOMUN.\nSo wait patiently for the judgment of your Lord, and be not like the companion of the fish, when he cried while he was in distress.\nلَّوْلَآ اَن تَدٰرَكَهُۥ نِعْمَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦ لَنُبِذَ بِالْعَرَآءِ وَهُوَ مَذْمُومٌ (49)\nLLAWLAA AAN TADAARAKAHU NEA’MATUN MMEN RRABBEHE LANUBEZA BIL-A’ARAAE WA HOWA MAZMOOMUN.\nWere it not that favor from his Lord had overtaken him, he would certainly have been cast down upon the naked Found while he was blamed.\nفَاجْتَبٰهُ رَبُّهُۥ فَجَعَلَهُۥ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِينَ (50)\nFAAJTABAAHU RABBUHU FAJAA’ALAHU MENAL AS-SAALEHEENA.\nThen his Lord chose him, and He made him of the good.\nوَاِن يَكَادُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ لَيُزْلِقُونَكَ بِاَبْصٰرِهِمْ لَمَّا سَمِعُوا۟ الذِّكْرَ وَيَقُولُونَ اِنَّهُۥ لَمَجْنُونٌ (51)\nWAAN YAKAADUL LAZEENA KAFARUL LAYUZLEQOONAKA BEAABSAAREHEM LAMMAA SAME-O’L KHASEYAR WAYAQOOLOONA INNAHUL LAMAJNOONUN.\nAnd those who disbelieve would almost smite you with their eyes when they hear the reminder, and they say: Most surely he is mad.\nوَمَا هُوَ اِلَّا ذِكْرٌ لِّلْعٰلَمِينَ (52)\nWA MAA HOWA ILLAA ZIKRUNW LLELA’AALAMEENA.\nAnd it is naught but a reminder to the nations.",
  "merits": "There are 52 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the one who recites this Surah will never face financial difficulties. Writing this Surah and tying it to any part of the body that is suffering from pain alleviates the pain."
